window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["0d"]={"https://theconversation.com/70-years-ago-the-suez-crisis-exposed-british-relative-decline-today-the-iran-conflict-could-be-doing-the-same-for-the-us-292833":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"9f43ffd2d37409afa3f38ccd541cb96507df74d3e2da878c941b23c3b2e8f972","read":"https://theconversation.com/70-years-ago-the-suez-crisis-exposed-british-relative-decline-today-the-iran-conflict-could-be-doing-the-same-for-the-us-292833","bytes":184733,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"70 years ago the Suez crisis exposed British relative decline. Today, the Iran conflict could be doing the same for the US","by":[{"n":"Eoin McLaughlin","r":"Professor in Economics, University College Cork"}],"pub":"2026-10-29T13:21:55Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Months after the US and Israel launched Operation Epic Fury against Iran, the Strait of Hormuz remains largely closed. The UK chose not to get directly involved in the conflict. Nonetheless, it has been exposed to the crisis through record-high diesel prices as well as a spike in inflation."]},{"k":"p","s":["This echoes an earlier crisis in the ",["Middle East","https://theconversation.com/topics/middle-east-361"],", as my ",["recent research","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/21582041.2026.2737244"]," illustrates."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seventy years ago, the Egyptian government nationalised the Suez canal, sparking the Suez crisis. The canal, which passes through Egypt from the Red Sea to the Mediterranean, was a vital link for ships travelling between Europe and Asia."]},{"k":"p","s":["After its completion in 1869 by a French-led company, the Egyptian government held a 44% stake in it. However, ",["financial difficulties","https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/480405/1873-by-ahamed-liaquat/9781529155853"]," forced Egypt to sell its shares to the British government in 1875, leaving Britain and France with substantial financial interests in the canal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the Egyptian nationalisation of the canal, France and Britain – together with Israel – invaded Egypt in an attempt to regain control of the vital waterway. But the invasion was a spectacular failure that was condemned by the international community. The crisis came to symbolise Britain’s loss of superpower status."]},{"k":"p","s":["Today, the US midterm elections are ",["increasing the pressure","https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/6116123-senator-calls-end-iran-conflict/"]," on the Trump administration over the current conflict. Elections in Israel have also had some bearing on the conflict, with ",["recent reports","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/netanyahu-reportedly-pressured-israel-military-attack-iran-runup-to-election"]," that Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu pushed for renewed strikes ahead of the election. Other ",["reports suggest","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/21/us/politics/us-israel-renewed-iran-strikes.html"]," that the US and Israel have drawn up plans to resume strikes after the elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1956, US presidential elections were also an important part of the calculus. But back then, Britain and France had assumed that the elections would distract the US from their actions. This was a miscalculation. In communication with UK Prime Minister Anthony Eden ",["the day after the vote","https://history.state.gov/historicaldocuments/frus1955-57v16/d545"],", US President Dwight D. Eisenhower was clear that his administration would not tolerate the UK, France and Israel’s continued actions. He demanded a negotiated settlement through the UN."]},{"k":"p","s":["The parallels between Suez and Hormuz go beyond the closure of two vital waterways. Both crises raise the same question: how far can geopolitical power outrun economic power?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Superpowers in decline"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1944, the American foreign policy professor William T.R. Fox coined ",["the term “super-power”","https://archive.org/details/superpowersunite0000will"],". He defined it as the consequence of “great wealth, great population, and favourable geographic position”. This is similar to how the historian ",["Phillips O’Brien","https://www.penguin.co.uk/books/461613/war-and-power-by-obrien-phillips-payson/9781405975612"]," defines great power today. Fox saw three superpowers at that time: the US, Britain, and the Soviet Union. He later ",["acknowledged","https://www.jstor.org/stable/40201883"]," that including Britain had been a mistake, primarily because of its relative decline against the US and later the rest of Europe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Arguably a similar shift is taking place today."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are arguments over what is the best measure of an economy, but on the basis of ",["purchasing power","https://www.cfr.org/articles/balancing-a-bigger-china"]," the shift is striking. China has moved from being a fraction of the size of the US economy in 1990 to being well ahead today."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the 19th century, Britain was the dominant global power and benefited from what economists call ",["“exorbitant privilege”","https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/738149"],". This was the ability to easily finance debt at favourable interest rates because sterling played a central role in the international monetary system. London was also the world’s ",["leading financial centre","https://global.oup.com/academic/product/the-london-stock-exchange-9780199242559?cc=gb&lang=en&"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But as Britain declined, this privilege gradually shifted towards the US. Its loss became particularly pressing during the Suez crisis as the pound came under ",["intense pressure","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0014498399907209"],". Similarly today, there are ",["signs of strain","https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/currencies/articles/us-sold-euros-save-yen-033819315.html"]," in the financial system that underpins American power."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the Suez crisis, Britain’s currency weakness and dependence on American financial support constrained its ability to act independently, despite its considerable military power."]},{"k":"p","s":["The crisis was also part of wider cold war geopolitics. An arms deal signed in 1955 between Egypt and the Soviet Union had upset the regional balance of power and ",["contributed to Israel’s decision","https://academic.oup.com/book/10548"]," to get involved in a preventative war."]},{"k":"p","s":["In response to the arms deal, the US withdrew financing for the Aswan Dam, a major infrastructure project on the River Nile. Then, in 1956, Egypt nationalised the Suez canal, sparking the crisis. British leaders sought to portray Egyptian president Gamal Abdel Nasser as ",["a 1930s dictator","https://hansard.parliament.uk/Commons/1956-09-12/debates/4726a68f-b54f-40af-b7cc-45a1a58a42a7/SuezCanal"],", intent on regional dominance."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US intervention in Iran has similar connotations. US secretary of war Pete Hegseth has presented the assassination of the Iranian leadership as necessary to prevent an existential threat from ",["“America’s mortal enemy”","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/12/pete-hegseth-antipathy-iran"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Geoeconomics","https://www.annualreviews.org/content/journals/10.1146/annurev-economics-092424-111952"],", the relationship between economics and geopolitics, also played a central role in the Suez crisis. The canal was a major conduit for Middle Eastern oil and there were fears that the nationalisation of the canal would disrupt UK oil supplies. But ironically, it was the decision to invade Egypt that led to a ",["shortage of oil and fuel rationing","https://www.google.co.uk/books/edition/Management_of_the_British_Economy_1945_6/3ckw3749Es4C?hl=en"]," in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["The wider cold war was a key factor in the US stance on events. The US did not want to be seen to be condoning imperial actions in Egypt while ",["condemning Russian imperialism in Hungary","https://www.simonandschuster.co.uk/books/Blood-and-Sand/Alex-von-Tunzelmann/9781847394606"],". Just as the Suez crisis needs to be understood in the context of the cold war, the current conflict should also be seen through the lens of “cold war II” geopolitics. Relations between the US and China have not thawed, while proxy wars bear similarities to the first cold war."]},{"k":"p","s":["Today, the US is increasingly stretched, most clearly seen in the depletion of its munitions. These were ",["already under pressure","https://www.ft.com/content/d7c1c90d-8b85-4044-a6b0-2a085f96714e"]," (in part because of its support for Ukraine) and have been ",["further reduced","https://www.cfr.org/articles/the-u-s-munitions-crisis"]," by the war with Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Suez crisis illustrates how political leaders can be slow to appreciate the economic constraints on their geopolitical ambitions. The US today is not Britain in 1956, yet the conflict in Iran has prompted questions about the ",["limits of American power","https://www.foreignaffairs.com/united-states/limits-american-power-william-mcraven"],". As its relative economic dominance is challenged, will the US also have to reconsider the extent of its global military commitments?"]}],"chars":6060},"https://theconversation.com/paraguays-bank-collapse-brought-down-a-president-and-exposed-as-myth-the-nations-status-as-a-dubai-of-south-america-296112":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"ee35fd13ef167f5a8f8fbe6b2fe851872a2abc5b3679e39895420ebe19cd4db0","read":"https://theconversation.com/paraguays-bank-collapse-brought-down-a-president-and-exposed-as-myth-the-nations-status-as-a-dubai-of-south-america-296112","bytes":193261,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Paraguay’s bank collapse brought down a president – and exposed as myth the nation’s status as a ‘Dubai of South America’","by":[{"n":"Joel E. Correia","r":"Associate Professor in Human Dimensions of Natural Resources, Colorado State University"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T13:43:39Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["It started on Nov. 3, 2026, when millions of Paraguayans trying to access the Ueno banking app found they ",["could no longer get their money","https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/what-is-ueno-bank-how-did-it-trigger-paraguays-political-crisis-2026-11-05/"],". In a matter of days, the financial situation escalated into political crisis, in which the country’s president was ousted, placed under house arrest and ",["charged with several corruption-related","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/06/world/americas/paraguay-president-removed-ueno.html"]," crimes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The political and financial crisis exposes a central contradiction in Paraguay’s ",["recent economic development","https://www.worldbank.org/ext/en/country/paraguay"],". Ueno, a bank celebrated for expanding financial access to ordinary Paraguayans, grew through unusually close relationships with political elites and public institutions. And while the Ueno crisis came as a shock, there were clear warning signs."]},{"k":"p","s":["As scholars with expertise in various aspects of Paraguay’s contemporary ",["political","https://nacla.org/paraguay-operation-condor-disappearance/"],", ",["economic and environment development","https://doi.org/10.1080/03066150.2017.1384726"],", we believe the collapse raises troubling questions about who benefits from financial modernization, who controls it and who bears the risks when it fails. The political relationships through which financial institutions grow, regulators exercise authority and public resources are entrusted to private companies are crucial national concerns, especially in a country that has presented itself internationally as a model of economic stability."]},{"k":"h","s":["A bank that grew faster than scrutiny"]},{"k":"p","s":["Founded as a digital lender in 2021, Ueno attracted customers with mobile banking and cash-back offers. Its expansion ",["brought useful services","https://www.forbesargentina.com/negocios/ueno-querer-ser-primer-unicornio-paraguayo-una-crisis-bancaria-hizo-renunciar-pena-n101802"]," to people underserved by conventional banks, including rural customers. Ueno also ",["expanded the credit card market to low-income customers","https://www.abc.com.py/economia/2025/04/13/evolucion-de-tarjetas-de-credito-en-el-sistema-bancario-paraguayo/"],", an unprecedented move compared to previously restricted banking practices."]},{"k":"p","s":["As Ueno expanded, Paraguay ",["increasingly attracted investors","https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2026-03-20/paraguay-why-a-little-known-trump-ally-is-attracting-investor-money"]," drawn by its low taxes, economic stability and business-friendly policies. Promoted by some as a “ ",["Dubai of South America","https://infonegocios.com.py/y-ademas/paraguay-tiene-el-potencial-de-convertirse-en-el-dubai-de-sudamerica-segun-referente-extranjero"],",” the country also became a magnet for ",["conservative influencers","https://elsurti.com/newsletter/paraguay-el-eden-de-los-conservadores-brasilenos"],", particularly from Brazil, who contrasted Paraguay’s economic model with the purported mismanagement of left-wing governments elsewhere in the region. Indeed, under President Santiago Peña, Paraguay has been one of Latin America’s most enthusiastic allies of the Trump administration and its expansive regional vision."]},{"k":"p","s":["But beneath the financial stability, Ueno stood at the precipice of a much deeper problem."]},{"k":"p","s":["The central bank finally acted after accounting adjustments left Ueno’s solvency ratio below half the legal minimum. But problems had surfaced earlier. That included a supervisory report ",["put out by the bank regulators in June 2026","https://www.abc.com.py/politica/2026/10/12/ueno-movio-us-146-millones-hacia-tres-empresas-vinculadas/"]," that described roughly US$146 million in loans to three companies linked to Grupo Vázquez, Ueno’s controlling shareholder. Some companies had been transferred to group employees; supervisors questioned the collateral and ultimate use of the funds."]},{"k":"p","s":["That these warning signs went unheeded raises a related question of why regulators didn’t have a better handle on the situation and were not better able to contain the exposure."]},{"k":"p","s":["In any case, Ueno’s problems were exposed in dramatic fashion on Nov. 2, when the central bank ",["placed Ueno","https://www.bcp.gov.py/web/institucional/w/banco-central-inicia-el-procedimiento-de-resolucion-de-ueno-bank/"]," into resolution, a process similar to bankruptcy but managed directly by Paraguay’s central bank. The lender, which says it has nearly 3 million customers – about half of the country’s population – halted transactions."]},{"k":"p","s":["The crisis quickly ensnared the governing party. Peña, an economist by training who was elected president in 2023 and had close ties to the bank, resigned on Nov. 5. The Senate then ",["voted unanimously","https://www.ultimahora.com/por-la-condena-congreso-fulmina-a-santiago-pena-y-lo-destituye-como-presidente-de-paraguay"]," to remove him from office, thereby stripping Peña of his parliamentary immunity. He was swiftly put under house arrest, charged with corruption and succeeded by his Vice President ",["Pedro Alliana, who was sworn","https://www.ultimahora.com/pedro-alliana-jura-como-presidente-tras-destitucion-de-santiago-pena"]," in to serve until 2028."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, the crisis has led to widespread protests, including outside Congress, with citizens accusing Peña and the ruling Colorado Party of “ ",["stealing” their savings","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-06/banking-crisis-plunges-paraguay-into-political-disarray/107355316"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["When the regulator knows the regulated"]},{"k":"p","s":["Part of the story of Ueno is a tale of the closeness between political and financial elites in Paraguay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carlos Carvallo chaired Ueno’s predecessor bank before Peña appointed him Paraguay’s central bank president in 2023. Carvallo ",["resigned on Nov. 3","https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/paraguays-central-bank-chief-resigns-presidents-request-digital-lender-crisis-2026-11-03/"]," and has since ",["been charged","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/06/world/americas/paraguay-president-removed-ueno.html"]," with the same corruption crimes as Peña. For its part, the Paraguayan central bank says Carvallo recused himself from any Ueno decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet the potential conflicts of interest ran much deeper. Peña previously directed Banco Basa, linked to Colorado Party leader and former President Horacio Cartes, who retains considerable influence and ",["was instrumental in helping push","https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/paraguay-ueno-bank-crisis-pena-resignation-9.7410656"]," Peña out of office. Finance Minister Carlos Fernández Valdovinos also served on Basa’s board. Local reporters had documented these ",["revolving-door relationships","https://elsurti.com/laprecisa/chequeo/2024/02/26/de-basa-y-ueno-a-cargos-publicos-estrategicos-que-manejan-la-economia-y-las-finanzas-del-pais/"]," early in Peña’s term."]},{"k":"p","s":["Peña reportedly held a ",["1.58% stake in Ueno Holding","https://www.abc.com.py/politica/2025/04/04/santi-aparece-como-socio-de-red-mimada-con-contratos-del-estado/"],", which shared its principal shareholder, Grupo Vázquez, with Ueno bank. His brother Francisco held shares in ",["Luxembourg-based U Holdings","https://www.abc.com.py/politica/2025/04/06/hermano-de-santi-era-parte-de-offshore-de-banco-favorito-dei-ips/"],", an indirect shareholder in the bank. ",["Another shareholder","https://www.abc.com.py/politica/2025/04/06/hermano-de-santi-era-parte-de-offshore-de-banco-favorito-dei-ips/"]," was Juan Carlos López Moreira, Cartes’ former chief of staff. Both brothers exited in 2025."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Peña has denied any wrongdoing","https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/paraguays-ex-president-pea-faces-prosecutors-after-impeachment-house-arrest-2026-11-07/"],", while prosecutors are examining allegations concerning his former business interests and his administration’s financial supervision."]},{"k":"p","s":["The inclusion of significant reserves of public funds made these connections especially consequential. Ueno held approximately ",["$850 million in public funds","https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/what-is-ueno-bank-how-did-it-trigger-paraguays-political-crisis-2026-11-05/"],", including ",["$355 million from the country’s social security system","https://www.abc.com.py/nacionales/2026/11/05/ueno-bank-ips-abrio-proceso-de-proteccion-de-sus-fondos-ante-el-bcp/"],", IPS, including health and retirement funds. It amounted to roughly 9% of IPS’s investment portfolio."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Peña-appointed chairman Jorge Brítez, IPS ",["relaxed eligibility requirements for bank deposits","https://www.abc.com.py/politica/2026/07/08/cambios-clave-en-el-ips-coincidieron-con-la-catarata-de-fondos-para-ueno-bank/"]," in 2023 and removed a capital-based exposure limit in 2024. Over the same period, its deposits at Ueno rose sharply. Grupo Vázquez’s technology firm ITTI won at least ",["$2.3 million","https://www.abc.com.py/economia/2025/03/12/contratos-de-itti-con-el-estado-se-triplicaron-durante-gobierno-de-pena-de-pequenas-facturaciones-paso-a-conseguir-g-17500-millones/"]," in state contracts after Peña took office, versus $675,000 before. ITTI attributed the increase to business expansion and denied a conflict of interest."]},{"k":"p","s":["Together these ties and regulatory changes raise important questions about ",["regulatory capture","https://www.jstor.org/stable/3003160"]," and other potential conflicts of interest."]},{"k":"h","s":["What the growth figures leave out"]},{"k":"p","s":["Paraguay’s economic gains are real. In August, the ",["International Monetary Fund projected 4.4%","https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2026/08/28/pr26280-paraguay-imf-executive-board-concludes-2026-article-iv-consultation"]," growth in 2026 following 6.6% in 2025. Moody’s granted the country’s debt ",["investment-grade status","https://ratings.moodys.com/ratings-news/425642"]," in 2024, and S&P ",["followed in","https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-12-17/s-p-lifts-paraguay-rating-to-investment-grade-joining-moody-s"]," 2025. Hydroelectric power exports, agriculture and new infrastructure continue to underpin the economy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Washington is also drawing Paraguay more firmly into its regional economic strategy. On Oct. 23, the country became the ",["26th signatory to the Pax Silica Declaration","https://www.mre.gov.py/paraguay-se-suma-a-la-declaracion-de-la-pax-silica/"],", an initiative involving critical minerals, hydropower and advanced computing infrastructure. While the announcement did not specify financing commitments, it shows how Paraguay’s resources and perceived political predictability are being positioned as strategic assets."]},{"k":"p","s":["But growth figures and credit ratings say little about who shapes financial oversight or bears the costs of banking failures. Paraguay’s ",["legacies of political patronage","https://doi.org/10.1086/695715"]," make it necessary to examine ",["political and corporate connections","https://www.abc.com.py/politica/2026/07/13/exsocios-de-pena-crecieron-en-paralelo-a-fondos-publicos/"]," and changes to ",["public-fund investment rules","https://elsurti.com/laprecisa/chequeo/2024/02/26/de-basa-y-ueno-a-cargos-publicos-estrategicos-que-manejan-la-economia-y-las-finanzas-del-pais/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["The social toll and the Colorado question"]},{"k":"p","s":["Paraguay has been here before. Between 1995 and 1998, ",["13 banks and 35 financial firms closed","https://www.elibrary.imf.org/display/book/9781589064201/ch002.xml"],", with direct costs estimated by the IMF at 10% to 13% of the country’s GDP. This preceded a smaller ",["bank crisis","https://www.hoy.com.py/nacionales/peirano-en-paraguay-la-quiebra-del-banco-aleman-y-otros-grandes-desfalcos-en-sudamerica"]," in the early 2000s. Both ordeals ",["exposed weak supervision","https://www.elibrary.imf.org/view/journals/087/2009/004/article-A001-en.xml"]," and ",["connected lending","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfs.2013.07.005"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Paraguay’s deposit guarantee, which ",["covers balances up to about $38,000","https://www.latintimes.com/paraguay-ueno-bank-collapse-president-resigns-600947"],", is meant to limit depositor losses, and the Paraguayan Central Bank insists that ",["failure is isolated","https://www.latintimes.com/paraguay-ueno-bank-resolution-political-crisis-600886"]," in the latest case. Yet account transfers have already ",["strained the system","https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2026-11-05/explainer-what-is-ueno-bank-and-how-did-it-trigger-paraguays-political-crisis"],", producing outages at several banking institutions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet for most Paraguayans, the crisis was experienced not through technical financial or macroeconomic indicators but at the stark level of seeing from their phones that they couldn’t access their money. Wages, pensions and savings ",["froze simultaneously","https://www.latintimes.com/paraguay-ueno-bank-collapse-president-resigns-600947"],". Young Ueno employees ",["burned their company cards","https://www.npr.org/2026/11/05/nx-s1-6030842/paraguay-president-impeached-bank-collapse"]," outside the Labor Ministry, demanding unpaid wages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Riot police used ",["pepper spray and rubber bullets","https://www.ibtimes.co.uk/paraguay-president-resigns-ueno-bank-crisis-1830483"]," against depositors marching on Congress. For small businesses that banked and paid staff through Ueno, the real economy stopped."]},{"k":"p","s":["This widespread anger challenges the ruling party’s claims to the economic vision they cite as the engine for future growth. Whether it leads to institutional change or a reshuffle within the Colorado Party remains an open question. The test is how Paraguayan legislators and regulators will move forward and whether they separate banking supervision and public deposits from partisan and business networks."]},{"k":"p","s":["In any case, the myth of the “Dubai of South America” has come under serious scrutiny. While the protests were noteworthy, the Colorado Party has for now managed to resolve its own internal crisis by quickly sacrificing key political elites, including the president."]},{"k":"p","s":["Marco Castillo Ph.D., Paraguayan sociologist, recent graduate and former director of research at the Center for Latin American, Latino and Caribbean Studies at Graduate Center CUNY, and Sheyla Rios Galeano, a Ph.D. Student in human dimensions of natural resources, Colorado State University, contributed to this article."]}],"chars":9360},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/portugal":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"45c8425f7db2d631630fc002960fec9313f64f4640d9bd3b2854aa6149b0e645","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/portugal","bytes":114645,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Portugal travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-12T11:00:21+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice also covers Madeira, Porto Santo and the Azores."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about the risks of travel, to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/portugal/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Portugal set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Portuguese Embassy in the UK","https://londres.embaixadaportugal.mne.gov.pt/en/the-embassy/contacts/embassy"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Portugal follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has either been reported lost or stolen or is damaged."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Portugal, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The requirements for ",["working in Portugal","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-portugal-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Portuguese border control you may need to show:"]},{"k":"li","s":["an onward or return ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof you have enough money for your visit"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting Portugal and need to extend your visa-free stay for exceptional reasons, such as a medical emergency, you must apply to AIMA using their ",["contact form (access is only available to users in Portugal)","https://contactenos.aima.gov.pt/contact-form"],". This does not apply to you if you’re the holder of a residence permit or long stay visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Portugal","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-portugal#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"p","s":["Prior to travelling to Portugal, you can use the EU’s ",["Travel to Europe mobile application","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/ees/Travel-to-Europe-mobile-app"]," to complete an entry questionnaire. The application is optional, but it can help you save time and speed up border checks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Non-resident children travelling to Portugal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children aged 17 and under travelling to Portugal alone, or with a person who is not their parent or legal guardian, must carry a letter of authorisation to travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Portuguese authorities have advised that the letter must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be signed and dated by the child’s parent or legal guardian"]},{"k":"li","s":["have the parent or guardian’s signature certified by a notary or solicitor"]},{"k":"li","s":["have the notary or solicitor’s signature legalised by the ",["Legalisation Office","https://www.gov.uk/get-document-legalised"]]},{"k":"li","s":["be accompanied by a copy of the child’s parent’s or guardian’s passport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure the letter includes:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the child’s full name, date of birth and passport number"]},{"k":"li","s":["the child’s dates of arrival and departure"]},{"k":"li","s":["the purpose of the visit"]},{"k":"li","s":["the address where the child will be staying"]},{"k":"li","s":["the name and passport number of the adult in Portugal who will be responsible for them during their stay"]},{"k":"li","s":["the full name, date of birth, passport number and contact details of the parent or guardian"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be prepared to show the letter of authorisation to border officials on arrival and departure from Portugal."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you bring a child to Portugal without a letter of authorisation, your entry will be delayed and may be refused."]},{"k":"p","s":["Teenagers aged 17 and under who travel alone, or with friends of the same age, and who are not being met on arrival by a parent or guardian, may be refused entry if they do not have a letter of authorisation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Resident children leaving Portugal"]},{"k":"p","s":["A child aged 17 or under who is resident in Portugal must carry a properly certified letter of authorisation if travelling without their parent or legal guardian. See more details in the ",["Living in Portugal guide","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-portugal#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see TravelHealthPro’s guides for ",["Portugal","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/181/portugal#Vaccine_Recommendations"],", ",["The Azores","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/18/azores-portugal#Vaccine_Recommendations"],", ",["Madeira","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/135/madeira-portugal#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," and Porto Santo."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are ",["strict rules about goods that can be brought into and taken out of Portugal","https://www.ana.pt/en/lis/passenger-guide/plan-your-trip/customs"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Portugal"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Portugal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Portugal cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political Situation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Political Demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations, political gatherings and marches are not uncommon, particularly in cities. While most demonstrations are peaceful, if you are near areas where they are taking place, you should remain aware of what is happening around you and follow the advice of the police and local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Strike action"]},{"k":"p","s":["Strike action that causes travel disruption, including at airports, can take place. Strikes can be announced at short notice. For updates on any disruption that may affect your travel plans, check the local news and follow the advice of your travel provider or tour operator."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to the risk of street crime. Take care on public transport and at crowded bus and tram stops. Thieves use distraction techniques and often work in teams. Look after your passport, money and personal belongings when travelling, checking in luggage at the airport or arranging car hire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not carry all your valuables in one place. Keep a copy of the photo pages of your passport somewhere safe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your accommodation has adequate security. Lock all doors and windows at night and when you go out. If you’re concerned about the security of your accommodation, speak to your tour operator or property owner, or contact the local police force:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Polícia de Segurança Pública (PSP)","https://www.psp.pt/Pages/onde-estamos.aspx"]," – the public security police force that covers cities"]},{"k":"li","s":["Guarda Nacional Republicana (GNR) – the national guard that covers smaller towns and rural areas"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Attacks and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks including sexual assaults, are rare but do occur. The risk is highest late at night around popular nightlife locations. In an emergency, call 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid splitting up from your friends, do not go off with people you don’t know and don’t let a friend walk back to their accommodation alone. Set up a group chat to keep in touch. Save the location of your accommodation on your maps app, so it’s easy to find or take a photograph of the name and address of your accommodation. For further tips and advice, see ",["TravelAware ‘Stick with your mates’","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/#stick_with_your_mates"]," and ",["getting help if you are a victim of crime abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and alcohol"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to the possible use of ‘date rape’ and other drugs including GHB and liquid ecstasy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Buy your own drinks and always keep them in sight to avoid them being spiked. Alcohol and drugs can reduce your vigilance, making you less in control. If you drink, know your limit. Drinks served in bars in Portugal are often stronger than those in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must provide photo ID if asked by a police officer. The police have the right to hold you at a police station until they have confirmed your identity. It is mandatory to carry ID when driving."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gambling"]},{"k":"p","s":["Gambling is only legal in places licensed by the government, such as official casinos. Games of chance, including bingo, are illegal if they’re held on unlicensed premises."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police may act on reports of illegal gambling in unauthorised premises without warning. You could be arrested, charged and fined or given a prison sentence. If in doubt, ask if the venue is licensed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Portugal have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Local laws governing public behaviour in Albufeira"]},{"k":"p","s":["The municipality of Albufeira has introduced a ",["Code of Conduct","https://www.cm-albufeira.pt/sites/default/files/RepositorioPublicacoes/2025/cma-regrascomp-regras13jun2025.pdf"]," which bans inappropriate behaviour in public places. Check out ",["the rules","https://www.cm-albufeira.pt/sites/default/files/RepositorioPublicacoes/2025/cma-regrascomp-regras13jun2025.pdf"]," that are now in force. If you break the rules, you could be fined on the spot from between 150 and 1800 euros."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Festivals, concerts and cultural events"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many large events are held in Portugal each year. Follow the advice of police and local authorities when attending events."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care of your valuables if attending a festival or large concert. See the ",["festival travel checklist","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/festival-travel-checklist"]," for more advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Beaches and swimming"]},{"k":"p","s":["Every year, people drown in the sea and in swimming pools in Portugal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming pools"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always supervise children. Keep small children within arms-reach in and around swimming pools, even if they can swim or there is a lifeguard present. Be particularly vigilant of children if you are staying in a villa with a private pool."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming in the sea. Always supervise children and keep small children within arms-reach. Don’t walk close to the water’s edge, especially along unsupervised stretches of beach. Waves can be unpredictable and some beaches have a strong undertow."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beware of rip tides, which can cause drowning. If you are caught in a rip tide, do not try to swim against it. Swim parallel to the coastline until you no longer feel the current, then try to swim towards the shore."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hidden rocks or shallow depths can cause serious injury or death. Do not dive into unknown water and do not swim at beaches where a river runs into the sea as there may be strong currents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Supervised beaches have a flag system. Make sure you understand the system and follow any warnings (a red flag means you must not enter the water, yellow means it’s only safe to paddle at the water’s edge). Take extra care and get local knowledge if there are no lifeguards, flags or signs."]},{"k":"p","s":["See further tips on ",["ABTA’s swim safe pages","https://www.abta.com/tips-and-advice/staying-safe-on-holiday/swim-safe"]," and ",["Water Safety on Holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cliff erosion"]},{"k":"p","s":["Look out for signs warning of cliff erosion. Falling rocks are a hazard, particularly in the Algarve. The authorities can fine people who ignore warning signs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking in Madeira and the Azores"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hiking in Madeira and the Azores can be challenging. Choose paths that suit your fitness and experience."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be prepared for narrow, uneven paths and heights. Wear suitable clothing and walking boots. Take extra care if it has rained, as the ground may be slippery and unstable. Check with your tour guide or local organiser that it is safe before you set off."]},{"k":"p","s":["Leave details of where you are going with your hotel reception and take a phone with you. Reduce the risk by walking with a group or following a guide."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more information about staying safe, walkway closures and access restrictions on ",["Visit Madeira","https://visitmadeira.com/en/travel-info/useful-information/advice-to-walkers/"]," and ",["Visit Azores","https://trails.visitazores.com/en/ethics-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Portugal, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Portugal guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/portugal/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Portugal. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring your own vehicle to Portugal for up to 183 days in any 12-month period. You must not use your vehicle for any other purpose than tourism or loan it to anyone else."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to stay longer, you must apply to the ",["Portuguese Customs authority","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/portugal-importation-of-motor-vehicles/importation-of-motor-vehicles-into-portugal"]," to have the car legally imported. You’ll be fined if you leave the country without your car."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Portugal, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["how long you can use your UK licence if you live in Portugal","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-portugal#driving-in-portugal"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tolls"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you understand ",["the toll system","https://www.portugaltolls.com/en"]," in Portugal and how to pay toll charges. If you think you may have used a toll road without paying, check the ",["Toll Payment Portal","https://www.pagamentodeportagens.pt/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extreme temperatures"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Summer months, there is a risk of higher than normal temperatures in Portugal. Check current weather forecasts and read about how to protect yourself on the ",["Portuguese Institute for Sea and Atmosphere website","https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fvigilance.meteofrance.fr%2Ffr&data=05%7C02%7CConsular.TravelAdviceTeam%40fcdo.gov.uk%7C0366784eef574311439408ded115d170%7Cd3a2d0d37cc84f52bbf985bd43d94279%7C0%7C0%7C639178088794764735%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=P3S92TN0dNxL2fJ29B0VcmYJzSaxmquyakIFUOla2fA%3D&reserved=0"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find advice on how to stay safe in hot weather from the ",["National Health Service (NHS)","https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/seasonal-health/heatwave-how-to-cope-in-hot-weather/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider and follow advice from local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an increased risk of wildfires from April to October when the weather is hot and dry. Wildfires can start anywhere in Portugal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. The Portuguese authorities may evacuate areas and close roads for safety reasons. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the ",["fire risk index","https://fogos.icnf.pt/rif/Stat_Global_Sensibilizacao_Riscolist2.asp?cmd=search&t=Stat_Global_Sensibilizacao_Risco&z_Distrito=%3D&x_Distrito=Lisboa&s_x_Distrito=s%3DqWdZQQfoL0nvgPIqYxyvA0PCo96bPEO64Kr_WevIwu5pe7gS7lE38M5vMEWB4vcON5LOTfPWSb3kt3hZcepo69CpZHWNk1isNAOYbIl7L3rPXSk4dNC49H7uk_nBT4YQIeBbNEPISi-VbXiJ8jLk_Sy0PwUj1zLCVekURxXZSKGWQXmkvvfaM7RR9FXFhOb06Now8ebhvpYMRmOA2By7UgZ7Doph1OWkVcioDKcYbmH02XBBg_hjdHZSW_r-e3cAX6DuzU7AjWsajA6lmlxI8jcsIjCyxpghUaJSu3X4UTE.%26d%3DDB%26f0%3DFpmwLCgZZEKoWy0G6I4vzcn_Ir0bBCh3Jj5oiA..%26t0%3D200%26fn0%3D&z_Concelho=LIKE&x_Concelho=&s_x_Concelho=s%3DKj1QSYU6d6vtOSr-LV4nbavzwBeNMOlXncgVBJ7Y7t0hLNQ-GhdE0PRVwyByw7LqACxm1qRIoFW-4nxrb8Y_WPCqDoCzZsssEFsPDaXOK55PDWfm2wIzlAi-in0l-IPNWms4TmuQ7E_FP09eYqrSf_VFRNpOrPPdWI_RJjahZKvEvwgZP3acG3QCG_MDqnR962GB3DG1USnjw0L6olALeFkj8DrZ-NIOuezWFg..%26d%3DDB%26f0%3DSV4E0VTr4yFHHgr8lM38VtPvTje7R9iqqtAHDA..%26t0%3D200%26fn0%3D%26f1%3DixGZmwftVA1p4rkBpeiELcB9I00YmTxBNt7hNQyUJAM.%26t1%3D200%26fn1%3D"]," for your location (in Portuguese)"]},{"k":"li","s":["familiarise yourself with ",["local safety and emergency procedures","https://aldeiasseguras.pt/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of the Portuguese authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["call the emergency services on 112 if you see a fire"]},{"k":"p","s":["Starting a fire, even if it is by accident, is illegal and you could get a fine or a prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information about active wildfires and forecasts, visit the Portuguese Met Office website for information on Portugal and Madeira."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Portugal. For more information, see the ",["Portuguese Met Office","https://www.ipma.pt/en/geofisica/sismicidade/"]," (for mainland Portugal) or the Earthquake Information and Surveillance Centre (for the Azores)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extreme weather warnings"]},{"k":"p","s":["For severe weather warnings, go to the ",["European Meteorological Services website","https://www.meteoalarm.org/en/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re feeling unwell, but it’s not an emergency, call:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mainland Portugal: (+351) 808 24 24 24, press 9 for English. If you have hearing loss and cannot hear on the phone, you can make contact by ",["videocall or webchat","https://www.sns24.gov.pt/contacto-acessivel-cidadao-surdo/"]," (Portuguese language website)."]},{"k":"li","s":["Madeira and Porto Santo: (+351) 800 24 24 20"]},{"k":"li","s":["Azores: (+351) 808 24 60 24"]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine information for Portugal","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/181/portugal#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Portugal","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/181/portugal#General_Information"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Changes to your routine when travelling, such as later nights, coping with heat and changes to your diet can have an impact on your medication. See the ",["Summer Proof Your Health","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/heat-travel-and-late-nights-how-summer-can-affect-your-medicines-and-how-to-stay-safe"]," campaign for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules around dispensing certain medicines in Portugal, including antibiotics. Keep any medication you bring or are prescribed in the original container with the prescription label."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK prescriptions are not recognised in Portugal. Carry enough medication for your visit and keep a few days’ supply in your hand luggage in case your checked-in baggage is delayed or lost."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need a repeat prescription, go to the nearest health centre or hospital A&E. You may have to pay for your medication."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to go to a pharmacy to get most medicines, though some non-prescription medication is sold at health stores in supermarkets and shopping centres. Find a pharmacy on the ",["Pharmacy Association website","https://www.farmaciasportuguesas.pt/catalogo/pesquisar-farmacias"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Portugal"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Portugal,","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/portugal-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Portugal, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Portugal","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-portugal-including-madeira"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"]," and ",["mental health support for UK nationals in Portugal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/portugal-mental-health-support-abroad/mental-health-support-for-british-nationals-in-portugal"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Portugal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Portugal"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Portugal"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Portugal"]," in Portugal"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Portugal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-portugal"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Portugal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/portugal-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of rape or sexual assault","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/portugal-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault/guidance-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault-in-portugal#:"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/portugal/british-embassy-lisbon"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/portugal/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Portugal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-portugal"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":23295,"change":"Removal of information on severe weather"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/vanuatu":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"6cd5473c9975d1b25832e522fdddfd9af75688729d450a1780a3965f0540df80","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/vanuatu","bytes":55153,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Vanuatu travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:02:48+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/vanuatu/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Vanuatu’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Vanuatu set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Vanuatu Department of Immigration and Passport Services","https://immigration.gov.vu/index.php"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Vanuatu, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with the ",["Vanuatu Department of Immigration and Passport Services","https://immigration.gov.vu/"]," for details of whether you need a visa in advance of travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Vanuatu guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/238/vanuatu#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Vanuatu","https://vanuatucustoms.gov.vu/index.php/customs"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Vanuatu"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Vanuatu, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of crime is generally low but there have been:"]},{"k":"li","s":["burglaries accompanied by violence"]},{"k":"li","s":["some instances of street crime and attacks on foreign nationals, including on tourists at nightclubs and bars in Port Vila"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take sensible precautions as you would in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should respect local customs, which are strictly observed, and religious sensitivities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not wear beachwear away from beaches and hotels."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for supermarkets to sell alcohol from midday on Saturday to 7am on Monday. However, clubs, bars and hotels may serve alcohol during these times."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kava drinking ceremonies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kava is a traditional drink in Vanuatu used in kava ceremonies, at kava bars (‘nakamals’) and at some hotels. Some nakamals, particularly outside of Port Vila, do not welcome women. Be wary of the effects of kava and consume it responsibly. Kava is ",["banned from entry to the UK","https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/importing-herbs-and-spices#:~:text=Kava%2Dkava,toxic%20effect%20on%20the%20liver."]," due to concerns about its health impacts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid all recreational drugs. Possession of even small quantities can lead to imprisonment and a large fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most people in Vanuatu will allow you to take their photograph, but you should always get permission first."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mobile phone coverage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ask your service provider if your mobile will work in Vanuatu. A 4G network is available but coverage varies across the country. You can also buy SIM cards from local phone companies Vodafone or ",["Digicel","https://www.digicelvanuatu.com/"],", including at Port Vila airport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visiting fees"]},{"k":"p","s":["Land ownership in Vanuatu is an important and often sensitive issue. If you travel off the beaten track, you may be trespassing unless you pay a ‘visiting fee’ to the landowner. At most beaches you will also be asked to pay an entry fee."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are legal in Vanuatu. However, showing affection in public may attract unwanted and negative attention and is likely to offend some people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming, diving or snorkelling in the sea as currents can be extremely strong. Coral reefs can easily cause cuts and scrapes. There are reports of water quality issues in some of the lagoons, and there are sharks in Vanuatu waters. Be cautious and follow the advice and instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water sports and scuba diving activities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many visitors to Vanuatu take part in water sports, including scuba diving and snorkelling without incident. However, water sports activities have on occasion led to injuries and deaths because of a lack of basic safety measures. To reduce risks:"]},{"k":"li","s":["use licensed water sports centres or operators"]},{"k":"li","s":["get any paperwork signed in advance"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you get a safety briefing before starting"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diving schools and rescue service standards are not always as high as in the UK. Check the dive operator’s credentials and make sure your insurance covers you."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce risks:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask your dive operator to explain what cover they offer before signing up"]},{"k":"li","s":["check safety equipment is available on the boat"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the operator’s plans for emergencies, including their ability to evacuate divers to the nearest hyperbaric chamber"]},{"k":"p","s":["Vanuatu has 2 hyperbaric recompression chambers, both in Port Vila."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society and the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents ",["watersports safety abroad guide","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Vanuatu, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Vanuatu. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many roads in Vanuatu are not properly surfaced. A lack of street lighting and the presence of pedestrians and animals makes roads particularly dangerous at night. Take extra care when driving at night, in heavy rain or after a prolonged dry period."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are below those in the UK and many vehicles, including public transport, are in a poor state of repair and may not be insured."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Air Vanuatu is currently not operating international or domestic flights. Check for messages from your travel agent in case of any changes or cancellations to your travel booking, including for code share tickets. Other airlines continue to operate flights to and from Vanuatu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel to outer islands is often on small local aircraft. Many domestic airports have basic or no facilities. Schedules may be changed or suspended at short notice due to weather conditions or ash clouds from volcanic activity."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Boat services between the islands are infrequent and can be unreliable. Boats travelling between the islands should have current sea-worthiness certificates, but many do not. Look into their safety before taking these services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["There was a significant earthquake in Port Vila on 17th December 2024 causing damage to buildings and local infrastructure. Some areas remain closed for safety reasons while assessments of damaged buildings are underway. Follow the advice of local authorities and do not enter closed areas for safety reasons. Some areas remain inaccessible following landslides."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many hotels and tourism operators are open for business, but some have been significantly impacted by the earthquake and are temporarily closed. Contact your travel agent, accommodation provider or airline for further information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vanuatu is in an active seismic region known as the ‘Ring of Fire’. Volcanic eruptions, earthquakes and tsunamis are possible. Tropical cyclones are also a risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["The tropical cyclone season in Vanuatu normally runs from November to May, but cyclones can happen throughout the year. During the cyclone season there is a greater risk of strong winds, heavy rains, flooding, landslides and road closures."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local news and check ",["World Meteorological Organization weather reports for Vanuatu","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/au/index.html"]," and the ",["Vanuatu Meteorology and Geohazards Department","https://www.vmgd.gov.vu/vmgd/index.php"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes and tsunamis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Vanuatu is in an earthquake zone and is prone to significant year-round seismic and volcanic activity, with an associated risk of tsunamis. There are over 2,000 seismic events reported each year. Most events are minor, but earthquakes over 5.0 magnitude happen regularly. Make sure you understand local safety procedures for earthquakes and tsunamis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["Vanuatu Meteorology and Geohazards Department","https://www.vmgd.gov.vu/vmgd/index.php"]," updates on seismic activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake or tsunami."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanoes"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Vanuatu there are active volcanoes on the islands of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ambae"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ambrym"]},{"k":"li","s":["Epi"]},{"k":"li","s":["Gaua"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lopevi"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tanna"]},{"k":"li","s":["Vanua Lava"]},{"k":"p","s":["Volcano alert levels can change unexpectedly, and you may not be able to access an island if a volcano is active."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel to an area with volcanoes:"]},{"k":"li","s":["contact the ",["Vanuatu Tourism Office","https://www.vanuatu.travel/en/"]," for the latest advice"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure your travel and medical insurance covers you"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local news and follow the advice of the local authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["For current volcano alert levels, see the Vanuatu Meteorology and Geohazards Department."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 115 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["For a fee, Promedical provide a 24-hour ambulance service in Port Vila and Luganville."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Vanuatu","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/238/vanuatu#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Vanuatu","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/238/vanuatu#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Vanuatu"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in Vanuatu are basic and limited in range and availability. There are medical clinics in Port Vila, some with Australian-trained GPs, which offer primary care. More serious cases will require evacuation to Australia or New Zealand. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad, medical evacuation and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Port Vila and need assistance from the UK government, call the British High Commission on (02)6270 6666."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Vanuatu"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 115"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 113"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 111 or 22222"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers in Vanuatu","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=vanuatu"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Vanuatu","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/vanuatu-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/vanuatu/british-high-commission-port-vila"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/vanuatu/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":14145,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/thabo-mbekis-legacy-in-south-africa-stronger-government-but-a-blurred-line-between-state-and-party-292384":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"09f57b628e5ee02a3c165d4e7aaea1f96f09888deaf7054c5674a4685dd6ec6f","read":"https://theconversation.com/thabo-mbekis-legacy-in-south-africa-stronger-government-but-a-blurred-line-between-state-and-party-292384","bytes":184584,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Thabo Mbeki’s legacy in South Africa: stronger government but a blurred line between state and party","by":[{"n":"Anthony Michael Butler","r":"Professor of Political Studies, University of Cape Town"}],"pub":"2026-10-09T13:07:48Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Evaluating national leaders is a difficult task. Citizens often judge presidents and prime ministers by simple measures like economic growth during their term, or personal character. However, these metrics are misleading and ignore the actual mechanics of political power."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am a ",["researcher","https://humanities.uct.ac.za/department-politics/contacts/anthony-butler"]," in public policy and politics. My ",["recent analysis","https://doi.org/10.1080/02589001.2026.2680959"]," offers a fresh four-dimensional framework to evaluate presidential leadership."]},{"k":"p","s":["This model examines how leaders handle tensions between:"]},{"k":"li","s":["symbolic authority and executive decision-making"]},{"k":"li","s":["heading a party and running a state"]},{"k":"li","s":["foreign policy and domestic pressures"]},{"k":"li","s":["formal authority and informal power networks."]},{"k":"p","s":["In each dimension there are opportunities for a skilled president to promote synergies. But there is also a risk of conflict and contradiction. I have previously used ",["this framework","https://doi.org/10.1111/psq.70035"]," to ",["explore Nelson Mandela’s presidency","https://theconversation.com/nelson-mandela-was-a-towering-global-symbol-but-how-effective-was-he-as-a-president-279599"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Nelson Mandela was a towering global symbol – but how effective was he as a president?","https://theconversation.com/nelson-mandela-was-a-towering-global-symbol-but-how-effective-was-he-as-a-president-279599"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Applying this framework to ",["Thabo Mbeki","https://www.presidency.gov.za/former-president-thabo-mvuyelwa-mbeki"],", who governed South Africa as president from 1999 to 2008, reveals a complex legacy. Mbeki was the country’s second post-apartheid president after Mandela. He was succeeded by ",["Kgalema Motlanthe","https://www.thepresidency.gov.za/former-president-kgalema-motlanthe"],", who served briefly before Jacob Zuma became president in 2009."]},{"k":"p","s":["I ",["found that Mbeki","https://doi.org/10.1080/02589001.2026.2680959"]," was a skilled and policy-focused president who introduced reforms that strengthened South African governance. However, his leadership contributed to institutional weaknesses that emerged more fully after he left office."]},{"k":"p","s":["He concentrated power and blurred the line between the ruling party and the state. Systems of political appointments and influence expanded during his presidency. These systems later made ",["state capture","https://theconversation.com/state-capture-in-south-africa-how-the-rot-set-in-and-how-the-project-was-rumbled-176481"]," easier – private financial interests could corrupt public institutions to steal public resources."]},{"k":"h","s":["Running government vs uniting the nation"]},{"k":"p","s":["South Africa has a ",["hybrid parliamentary system","https://unisapressjournals.co.za/index.php/Politeia/article/view/3148"]," with some presidential features. The national assembly elects a president rather than a prime minister. This figure combines two roles: acting as head of government – managing cabinet leaders of national executive departments – and as a head of state charged with uniting the nation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mbeki managed the head of government role with great technical skill."]},{"k":"p","s":["He centralised strategic planning within the presidency and personally drove the creation of a modern national treasury. Working with ",["finance minister Trevor Manuel","https://www.polity.org.za/topic/trevor-manuel"],", Mbeki stabilised the economy (blessed with ",["favourable global conditions","https://www.penguinrandomhouse.co.za/product/presidents-6162738/"],"). Economic growth averaged over ",["4% annually","https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG?locations=ZA"],", up from less than 3% under Mandela. His administration reduced public debt, expanded infrastructure and extended welfare grants to millions of poor citizens."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, Mbeki failed as a unifying head of state during the ",["health crisis of HIV and Aids","https://doi.org/10.1093/afraf/adi036"],". Rather than bringing people together to fight the epidemic, he ",["rejected","https://doi.org/10.1093/afraf/adi036"]," scientific consensus on the cause of the disease. He questioned the safety of life-saving antiretroviral medication and delayed public distribution. One ",["study","https://www.ovid.com/jnls/jaids/abstract/10.1097/qai.0b013e31818a6cd5%7Eestimating-the-lost-benefits-of-antiretroviral-drug-use-in?redirectionsource=fulltextview"]," estimated that earlier access to antiretroviral treatment would have saved over 300,000 lives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mbeki ",["held his position","https://doi.org/10.1093/afraf/adm087"]," despite intense public protest and global condemnation. His stance demonstrated a failure to provide national leadership when it was most needed."]},{"k":"h","s":["Serving the party vs strengthening the state"]},{"k":"p","s":["The second structural tension involves the divide between the ruling party and state administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mbeki rose through the ",["exiled ranks","https://www.jonathanball.co.za/product/thabo-mbeki-the-dream-deferred/"]," of the African National Congress (ANC). After taking power in 1994, the party struggled to turn a political organisation into a party of government. At its 1997 national conference, the party adopted a policy document on its “ ",["strategy and tactics","https://www.anc1912.org.za/50th-national-conference-policy-documents-strategy-and-tactics-as-amended-by-conference/"],"”. The document described constitutional democracy as an interim step towards a broader national democratic revolution."]},{"k":"p","s":["To secure control, the party started using a “cadre deployment” policy that bore Mbeki’s intellectual imprint. Cadre deployment meant placing loyal party members into top positions across government departments, municipalities and state companies. It severely damaged state capacity. Civil servants became answerable to party bosses rather than professional standards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["South Africans who blow the whistle face retaliation and murder: their stories over five decades","https://theconversation.com/south-africans-who-blow-the-whistle-face-retaliation-and-murder-their-stories-over-five-decades-266499"]]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["study on party dominance","https://doi.org/10.1080/00344890902945681"]," notes that long-ruling party tenure erodes public accountability. Mbeki centralised policy inside his personal office and suppressed party dissent. When he tried to retain party control in 2007, the party base rejected his ambition for an additional term and ",["voted him out of office","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2008/sep/22/southafrica"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Leading abroad vs domestic interests"]},{"k":"p","s":["The third tension pits international diplomacy against domestic priorities. Mbeki ",["reshaped foreign policy","https://www.ohioswallow.com/9780821422748/thabo-mbeki/"]," around ",["pan-Africanism","https://www.britannica.com/topic/Pan-Africanism"],", a political idea promoting African economic unity and self-reliance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mbeki centralised foreign relations within the presidency. He helped create the New Partnership for Africa’s Development ( ",["Nepad","https://au.int/en/nepad"],"), a plan to integrate African economies fully into the global economy. He also ",["led the transformation","https://au.int/en/cpau1"]," of the Organisation of African Unity into the African Union."]},{"k":"p","s":["He built ",["strong diplomatic ties","https://ujcontent.uj.ac.za/esploro/outputs/journalArticle/Continuity-and-change-in-the-foreign/9910109907691"]," with developing nations across the global south, most strikingly through the India-Brazil-South Africa Dialogue Forum. These efforts ",["expanded international trade","https://www.jstor.org/stable/4006691?seq=1"]," and secured South Africa a ",["non-permanent seat","https://www.hrw.org/news/2018/06/11/south-africa-secures-seat-un-security-council-third-time"]," on the United Nations security council."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet Mbeki’s foreign policy created severe problems at home through his response to neighbouring Zimbabwe. As Zimbabwe suffered ",["political repression and economic collapse","https://ujcontent.uj.ac.za/esploro/outputs/journalArticle/Continuity-and-change-in-the-foreign/9910109907691"],", Mbeki adopted quiet diplomacy. This relied on private persuasion rather than public criticism."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mbeki ",["protected","https://issafrica.org/iss-today/thabo-mbekis-quietly-destructive-policy-on-zimbabwe"]," President Robert Mugabe and endorsed flawed Zimbabwean elections. This policy shielded a repressive regime. The later collapse of Zimbabwe’s economy forced millions of desperate citizens into South Africa, fuelling ",["violent xenophobia","https://theconversation.com/xenophobia-in-south-africa-states-complicity-with-gangs-and-vigilantes-is-threatening-its-ability-to-govern-285280"]," after Mbeki had left office."]},{"k":"h","s":["Formal vs informal influence"]},{"k":"p","s":["The final tension lies between formal legal powers and informal networks of influence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["South African constitution","https://www.gov.za/documents/constitution/constitution-republic-south-africa-04-feb-1997"]," grants the president expansive appointment powers over cabinet ministers, judges, police chiefs and tax officials. Mbeki used these powers to ",["place loyalists","https://doi.org/10.1080/02589001.2026.2680959"]," across critical state agencies."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the same time, rising campaign costs forced the ruling party to seek private funding. Under Mbeki, fundraising events sold corporate access to government ministers in exchange for party donations. This helped the party fund effective participation in national elections but compromised the integrity of government decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["South Africa’s police serve the ANC insiders, not the people: here’s how it happened","https://theconversation.com/south-africas-police-serve-the-anc-insiders-not-the-people-heres-how-it-happened-261301"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Mbeki also expanded a variant of ",["Black Economic Empowerment","https://www.researchgate.net/publication/265432768_Black_Economic_Empowerment_since_1994_Diverse_hopes_and_differentially_fulfilled_aspirations"],", a state policy that gave Black citizens ownership stakes in businesses to redress apartheid inequality. Established corporations used the policy to ",["grant shares","https://www.researchgate.net/publication/265432768_Black_Economic_Empowerment_since_1994_Diverse_hopes_and_differentially_fulfilled_aspirations"]," to politically connected individuals in exchange for influence in government."]},{"k":"p","s":["One ",["study on economic transformation regimes","https://doi.org/10.1353/trn.2022.0011"]," found that empowerment policies can turn into patronage networks for ruling elites. The African National Congress even established its own investment firm, ",["Chancellor House","https://www.academia.edu/82918549/Financing_the_ANC_Chancellor_House_Eskom_and_the_dilemmas_of_party_finance_reform"],", which won multibillion-rand state contracts."]},{"k":"p","s":["While Mbeki personally faced no corruption charges, his administration built a system of informal patronage and money politics. This system created an architecture of dysfunction that enabled ",["widespread state capture","https://pari.org.za/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/PARI-Summary-The-Zondo-Commission-A-bite-sized-summary-v360.pdf"]," under his successor, Zuma."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mbeki’s mixed legacy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Evaluating presidential leadership requires looking beyond personal character or short-term economic prosperity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mbeki proved himself a highly capable administrative manager. He maintained fiscal discipline and expanded South African influence across the continent. Yet his centralising leadership style, party deployment policies and informal patronage networks weakened democratic institutions."]}],"chars":7908}};
